Hanzi Wallet 1.1.0

Application source code is MIT licensed (see LICENSE).

Character data are derived from hanzi-writer-data 2.0.1 by David Chanin and
contributors, itself derived from Make Me a Hanzi by Shaunak Kishore and
contributors, and from fonts released by Arphic Technology Co., Ltd.

https://github.com/chanind/hanzi-writer-data
https://github.com/skishore/makemeahanzi

Stroke data and derivative trained weights are distributed with the Arphic
Public License, included at public/data/ARPHICPL.txt. The source data are
available in the named upstream projects; this repository includes the exact
500 character templates used for training and a reproducible training script.

Changes: 500 characters selected and repackaged in public/data/templates.json;
median coordinates converted from 1024-unit, upward-y character space to a
normalized downward-y plane. Stroke outlines are preserved. Synthetic pen
trajectory augmentations are used to generate the derivative neural weights.
The vocabulary's Spanish glosses were adapted from the user-provided prototype.

The geometric app icon is original. Interface design is inspired by Apple's
public Liquid Glass design language; no Apple proprietary assets are bundled.

